    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45575" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐωχ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good cheer, feasting</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1009
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aff.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖν τὴν εὐ</span>. to
			hold the <i>wake</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3028
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Ephesus</span>): in pl.,
			<i>festivities</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				216
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				329a
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, <i>supply of provisions</i> for an army, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.92.9
			</span></i>; <i>plenty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.38.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων εὐωχίαι</span>
			<i>feasts</i> of reason, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				4.3.6
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>).</div>
